 an English barrister who became the first governor of the Colony of Vancouver Island in 1849.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/richard-chancellor"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/richard-chancellor.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Richard Chancellor</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Richard Chancellor was an English navigator who in 1553 sailed with Sir Hugh Willoughby's expedition in search of a north-east passage to China.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/richard-clement-moody"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/richard-clement-moody.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Richard Clement Moody</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Richard Clement Moody was a British officer of the Royal Engineers who served as the first governor of the Falkland Islands from 1841 to 1848.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/richard-de-clare-2nd-earl-of-pembroke"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/richard-de-clare-2nd-earl-of-pembroke.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Richard de Clare, 2nd Earl of Pembroke</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Richard de Clare, known as Strongbow, was a Cambro-Norman lord who led the Anglo-Norman invasion of Ireland.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/richard-francis-burton"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/richard-francis-burton.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Richard Francis Burton</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Sir Richard Francis Burton was a British explorer, soldier, linguist and writer.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/richard-harliston"><span class="enc-name">Richard Harliston</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Sir Richard Harliston was an English naval commander and Yorkist supporter who recovered Jersey for Edward IV.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/richard-i-of-capua"><span class="enc-name">Richard I of Capua</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Richard I was a Norman leader of the Drengot family who became count of Aversa in 1049 and prince of Capua in 1058, after taking the city from its Lombard ruler.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/richard-i-of-england"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/richard-i-of-england.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Richard I of England</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Richard I of England, known as Richard the Lionheart, was King of England from 1189 to 1199 and a leading commander of the Third Crusade.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/richard-ii-of-england"><span class="enc-name">Richard II of England</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Richard II was King of England from 1377 to 1399, succeeding his grandfather Edward III at the age of ten.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/richard-ii-duke-of-normandy"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/richard-ii-duke-of-normandy.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Richard II, Duke of Normandy</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Richard II, called the Good, was ruler of Normandy from 996 to 1026, the son of Richard I.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/richard-iii-of-england"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/richard-iii-of-england.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span cla